Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||07-05-2000||03:30 AM||||Ok I think I finally decided on yellow over navy blue metalic.  I rember somebody posted a ferrari modena and a we found a store that can mix it in (ppg).  But all that is listed is this color.  Are alll yellow ferraris the same yeloow?  When I was looking at paint samples the ones that stood out were a "gm yelow" and the yellow that they are putting on the dodge trucks.  All the rest were kind of dull or had an orange tint to it.  But also the new body style yellow mustangs are a pretty yellow.  for those of you that have gone with yellow what code did you use?  Also what manufacturer did you use?  As far as I know PPG is the best.  Does anyone have any opinions on this??  I need to find this stuff out pretty soon because I am near through sanding.  If anyone has pics of thier yellow fieros can yall please post them.<BR>thanks in advance<BR>Dan||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||07-05-2000||09:13 AM||||I painted one of my cars '87 Porsche Summer Yellow- I cant remember the code, but it is the only yellow for that year. It was a very bright, pure yellow that borders on being a florescent color.<BR>At that time we used Dupont BC/CC, but have since switched to PPG. Your paint supplier should also be able to mix you a custom yellow and not add anything but the yellow pigments.<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 07-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||07-05-2000||10:29 AM||||I painted an 87 GT using PPG and the paint supplier has the co;or chip. The color is an 88 Fiero yellow and that color was only in 88.<BR>Check out the Yellow Fiero on my web site. Their is a silver car and next to it is the yellow car. They are both the same car. <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/photos.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/photos.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 07-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||07-05-2000||10:41 AM||||I used Corvette Competition Yellow WA9804 -don't know brand of paint used.||||reg||1
